    "context": "Artemis uses paired 16-bit RAM modules on a 32-bit memory bus. PRO uses the same high-density module family with larger populations. Native ERA applications use AIONix; the optional Z80 card remains a separate execution path qualified only for Artemis.",
    "memory_note": "Functional address map. The selected replaceable video card contains its controller, 16 or 32 KiB display DRAM, independent 1 KiB sprite SRAM and internal buffers. Host MMU, DMA and system refresh remain outside the card. Numeric apertures are not yet assigned.",
    "ram_note": "Choose an explicit matched-bank population. Low- and high-density configurations with the same capacity are distinct. Expanded populations and 1 MiB board capacity are design targets pending timing, loading and power qualification; they are not extra shipping bundles.",
    "bundle_note": "Bundle contents follow the selected catalog offer and are independent of the exploratory RAM and networking controls. Items absent from the bundle record are not assumed to be included.",
    "notes": {
      "hardware": "Select a block to inspect the processor, RAM, custom chipset, storage and expansion interfaces. Lines show functional relationships, not a wiring or bus-timing specification.",
      "peripherals": "Compatible devices are grouped by interface. Dashed connections denote optional devices; a monitor listed as a bundle option is included only in bundles naming that monitor. Introduction dates are shown for later offerings.",
      "software": "Explore the native AIONix services, Business Tools, compatible software and C development tools. The optional Z80 module is distinct from native ERA recompilation.",
      "memory": "Follow virtual addressing through the MMU to physical memory resources. Select RAM capacity to inspect module population. No undefined address ranges are invented.",
      "bundles": "Select an offer to see its computer configuration, devices, software and services. Planned availability remains explicitly labeled."
    },
